# W3_PLUGIN_MODEW_PACK

TYPE: W3MD_MANIFEST  
STATUS: TEMPLATE_DRAFT  
SCOPE: W3_PLUGIN / MODEW_PACK / CAPABILITY_BUNDLE  
OWNER: BBX19  
MUTATED: false  
EXECUTION_ALLOWED: false  
REVIEW: true  

---

## INTENT

Define a reusable W3 capability bundle that can be read by humans, AI agents, modules, and W3API without granting execution permission by default.

---

## CONTEXT

This manifest is used when a capability needs to be packaged as a W3-style pack.

Examples:

```text
- W3API Gateway pack
- Cross-L Planner pack
- Hospitication Intake pack
- WE PAPER Library pack
- Table-X Matrix pack
- Modew Dynamic pack
```

---

## W3LGU 5-LINE DRAFT

```text
MEM: W3_PLUGIN_MODEW_PACK; REF:w3_tool_store/modew_pack_template.
PATCH: package capability as reusable bounded pack.
LAW: mutated:false; execution_allowed:false; review:true; boundary_first.
EVENT: pack/request -> skills/agents/commands/hooks -> return_contract.
RETURN: state, reason, trace, mutated, review, capability_summary.
```

---

## STRUCTURE

```text
pack identity
skills
agents
commands
hooks
assets
mpcp/mcp hints
boundary
return contract
```

---

## BOUNDARY

Allowed:

```text
- describe capability
- provide templates
- provide commands as patterns
- provide hooks as observation points
- provide return contract
- support planning and review
```

Denied by default:

```text
- direct execution
- truth mutation
- repo write
- direct merge
- secret access
- network action without explicit bridge
```

---

## OUTPUT CONTRACT

Any pack based on this template should return at minimum:

```text
state
reason
trace
mutated
review
capability_summary
```

---

## PHILOSOPHY

Use external plugin structures as materials, not as masters.

```text
We do not copy the form.
We extract useful organs.
W3 gives them new role, boundary, and meaning.
```

END
